{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags","id":1377726,"title":"Wealth and the absurd sparsity of Weapon Tags","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-01T06:50:14-07:00","id":1377726,"title":"Wealth and the absurd sparsity of Weapon Tags","content":"I haven't seen this written on here, so, I'm creating a post to say that the Wealth system as it relates to weapons is bonkers. According to the book, a weapon starts with 1 tag and you can add another per dot of wealth you possess. They state that every weapon should be custom designed. However, if you do this, it requires wealth three to get a knife, and only Bezos can afford an assault rifle (4 tags and 7 tags respectively). In the Trinity book, the upper middle class can afford one knife while the rich can afford a so many more. In this universe the movie &quot;Knives Out&quot; showcases the opulence of the family by literally having them hold out their knives during their shots.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the best solution is, but I lean toward two tags to start with and two tags per dot of Wealth. I'm going this route to bring it a bit more in line with reality and because the writer of the section says that the &quot;weapon should be as special and unique as the character itself.&quot; How do other people feel about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25211-justinfernal","name":"justinfernal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25211_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T09:26:41-07:00","id":1377753,"title":"","content":"I haven't really run into this as an issue. The example weapons have more tags than they need in many cases. Lower Wealth characters could easily get less potent versions. Knife is actually a great example as your average survival knife isn't going to really justify the Concealable or Thrown tags, dropping it down it 1 tag point and thus available to Wealth 0 characters.<br /> <br /> While in the Wealth section instead of the weapon section, you can always take on a Complication equal to the dots you're missing to get your hands on something. A Wealth 2 character that wants a weapon that costs Wealth 3 to get? Their Wealth drops to 1 for the rest of the session and they take a 1 dot Complication to deal with in getting it (or a future financial matter if the SG is feeling that will be relevant).<br /> <br /> And characters can get equipment through their Paths as well.<br /> <br /> So I've never really seen the need to modify this.<br /> <br /> Serious combat weapons are major purchases for most people. Your average gun-totting American probably has 3-4 functional guns that they've purchased/replaced over years, not in one run out to the store. For most people a $500 to $1,000 purchase is no small deal for their budget (and that's on the low side for a gun).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T09:39:02-07:00","id":1377756,"title":"","content":"In addition to Heavy Arms' excellent points, you also have the ability to take an Artifact for a Super-Science weapon. They don't quite get an abundance of tags, but you can save on Quality or other enhancement bonus tags by using the gimme enhancement from Super-Science weapons. This will really help you get that &quot;special weapon&quot; vibe.<br /> <br /> Another note, in \u00c6on, weapons get 4 additional tags for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:25:28-07:00","id":1377779,"title":"","content":"My personal house rule for that is Wealth +2 tags for weapons and armors (Not counting the minimum of 1 Soft armor). I have to add that I never used it, as usually the characters have equipment related to their paths and hardly have to buy anything too expensive (maybe a car or a ship, but in this case the cost is balanced).<br /> <br /> Additionally, the enhancements of Assault Rifles don\u2019t fit the tags, I would remove the Quality 2, reducing the total to 5 tags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-01-2020, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:33:51-07:00","id":1377783,"title":"","content":"This might be me, but I'm not a fan of ludonarrative dissonance. I can understand what you're saying regarding that there are ways of acquiring the weapons through other paths than wealth, or, that wealth with problems is definitely something fun and fixes some issues. I also like that in another book it discusses getting 4 additional tags is a good idea. However, I think saying that there's a way around the base system so that it's fun isn't a good solution to the base system not being correct and that the Aeon book is already addressing the idea that there is a problem. Also, I think saying what if we didn't even just look at weapons and instead had artifacts also showcases there being a problem. In the real world, low-income people can and do get knives and most knives can be hidden on your person fairly easily, and, can be thrown. Additionally, the knife starts with 4 tags, so, even dropping the two tags mentioned above actually still puts it outside the range of wealth zero unless they have a complication, which is a bizarre idea to me, as most people, including the homeless, have a way of acquiring a knife. Again, just looking at the weapons section in the book, it says that the weapon should be as unique as the character itself. But, just looking at the actual weapon section, not using workarounds, if you can only acquire a regular assault rifle through complications, then that means that the mechanics of that section does not match the flavor of the same section. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of the way Aeon does it. Is that how most people are running it even if they aren't playing Aeon? <br /> <br /> Again, I'm not looking for &quot;what if we just ignore the section and use different things.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25211-justinfernal","name":"justinfernal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25211_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:36:51-07:00","id":1377784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1377779#post1377779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal house rule for that is Wealth +2 tags for weapons and armors (Not counting the minimum of 1 Soft armor). I have to add that I never used it, as usually the characters have equipment related to their paths and hardly have to buy anything too expensive (maybe a car or a ship, but in this case the cost is balanced).<br /> <br /> Additionally, the enhancements of Assault Rifles don\u2019t fit the tags, I would remove the Quality 2, reducing the total to 5 tags.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Quality is there to increase the Enhancement from 1 to 2. So far I haven't had to have any players buy anything either, however, I want to make sure I have a good response for them if they try to rather than just giving a shrug and saying &quot;well, don't try to buy weapons.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25211-justinfernal","name":"justinfernal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25211_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:39:54-07:00","id":1377785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>justinfernal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1377784#post1377784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Quality is there to increase the Enhancement from 1 to 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check the Two Handed tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T17:08:20-07:00","id":1377825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1377785#post1377785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check the Two Handed tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two-handed tag says that it gives +1 enhancement toward inflicting the Injury condition. That would not apply toward the initial roll or anything else. This means that with a two-handed weapon, when you hit, you have a free enhancement to apply toward injury, but not toward disarming or similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25211-justinfernal","name":"justinfernal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25211_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:06:49-07:00","id":1377836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>justinfernal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1377783#post1377783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be me, but I'm not a fan of ludonarrative dissonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK... but just tossing out that phrase doesn't really mean much. Ludonarrative dissonance, like suspension of disbelief, and similar concepts, are also things on a scale. It's not a binary. Pretty much all games have some level of disconnect between narrative and game-play (though ludonarrative dissonance is a bigger deal in video games compared to TT RPGs since video games craft a narrative for you while you're expected to craft your own narrative in a TT RPG).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also like that in another book it discusses getting 4 additional tags is a good idea. </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that's for a future setting to represent a higher level of tech available (esp. after the impact of super-science).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I think saying that there's a way around the base system so that it's fun isn't a good solution to the base system not being correct and that the Aeon book is already addressing the idea that there is a problem. </div> </div> </div>The base system is fine. It's not &quot;incorrect.&quot; As well, Paths being a source of equipment rather than Wealth is also part of the base system (and is more central as a mechanic than weapon creation). Aeon doesn't &quot;address&quot; that there is a problem, it just changes the numbers for the above cited reason. Aeon's changes are something that counters ludonarrative dissonance: equipment is mechanically better for the cost in the future of TC as the narrative says technology is significantly more advanced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the real world, low-income people can and do get knives and most knives can be hidden on your person fairly easily, and, can be thrown. </div> </div> </div>There's a huge difference between a combat knife, and a 3-inch blade you keep for EDC.<br /> <br /> And you can throw anything. Most knives are not designed for being thrown and do not justify the thrown tag to avoid penalties for throwing things that aren't meant to be thrown as weapons.<br /> <br /> You can make a Wealth 0 Knife that's an accurate model of most knives people have that are sturdy enough to actually hold up to a fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...which is a bizarre idea to me, as most people, including the homeless, have a way of acquiring a knife. </div> </div> </div>Right. They don't buy them with a pile of cash they don't have. That's why the game lets you get equipment without having to go through Wealth. If you steal a knife, you don't need to have Wealth = tag value - 1 to steal it... because that would be really bad ludonarrative dissonance. If you still a knife you just get it. If you're poor and you do a some favors to some sketchy folks to get your hands on a gun.... again... you don't have to go through Wealth because that wouldn't make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, just looking at the actual weapon section, not using workarounds, if you can only acquire a regular assault rifle through complications, then that means that the mechanics of that section does not match the flavor of the same section. </div> </div> </div>Well, considering most people live in places where automatic weapons are illegal... I'm not sure that's the case at all. Starting with an automatic weapon should come with some complications attached to it.<br /> <br /> This argument also not very clear. You can customize your weapon using whatever tags suit you to make it individualized. Whether you can afford weapons with 3 tags, or 6 tags, your ability to customize them doesn't change. The flavor and mechanics mesh fine, even if you don't agree with the cost scheme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I'm not looking for &quot;what if we just ignore the section and use different things.&quot; </div> </div> </div>None of us are saying that. TC isn't a system where you can analyze sections in isolation though. It's not built for that kind of thinking. The weapon creation system was written with the Path equipment rules in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:17:00-07:00","id":1377859,"title":"","content":"Enhancements are never applied to initial roll. You can only add enhancements if you get at least one success in the dice.<br /> <br /> Your point is valid anyway for sure, but in the Katana description just below, it seams it is applying anyway to the enhancement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:09:50-07:00","id":1377872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>justinfernal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1377783#post1377783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the base system not being correct and that the Aeon book is already addressing the idea that there is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn\u2019t what\u2019s happening. Aeon isn\u2019t saying there\u2019s a problem with the base system, it\u2019s saying 100+ years of scientific development (including several years of super-powered R&amp;D) tends to pack more things into equipment. <br /> <br /> Or put it another way - my car today has a lot more features and equipment than a car of 100 years ago, but they both cost around the same compared to wages of the time. But I\u2019m not going to say the system is broken if a game set in the Adventure! era doesn\u2019t give me a car with air bags, ABS, cruise control, traction control, streaming music player etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:36:29-07:00","id":1378019,"title":"","content":"I was gonna respond, but then Heavy Arms and Bunyip did it perfectly for me. Cheers.<br /> <br /> To try and contribute further though, consider this Wealth and Cost abstraction as player facing guidance. The actual Cost of something in game has a number of factors, Supply/Demand, economics yadda yadda. So even though an assault rifle has a rather high Cost for character generation or path Access, there could be a mostly automated factory churning them out so they can be purchased relatively cheaply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:52:24-07:00","id":1378093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1378019#post1378019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was gonna respond, but then Heavy Arms and Bunyip did it perfectly for me. Cheers.<br /> <br /> To try and contribute further though, consider this Wealth and Cost abstraction as player facing guidance. The actual Cost of something in game has a number of factors, Supply/Demand, economics yadda yadda. So even though an assault rifle has a rather high Cost for character generation or path Access, there could be a mostly automated factory churning them out so they can be purchased relatively cheaply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention the only place you can buy an automatic weapon in Wallmart is US (and not all the states), any other place in the world will require some good reason to have one for personal use (I believe here in Brazil you can\u2019t buy one legally, period).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:17:29-07:00","id":1378129,"title":"","content":"It's illegal in the USA to buy new automatic weapons. Outside of specific professions, the general public can only legally own an automatic weapon if it was made before the mid-80's law that banned them for civilian use. You can buy weapons that can be modified if you know how, and there's issues with things like bump-stocks, but you can't just walk into a store that sells guns and buy the equivalent of the assault rifle in TC core. No amount of cash is going to let you walk into a store and buy something they can't even legally keep in stock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:34:21-07:00","id":1378151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1378129#post1378129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's illegal in the USA to buy new automatic weapons. Outside of specific professions, the general public can only legally own an automatic weapon if it was made before the mid-80's law that banned them for civilian use. You can buy weapons that can be modified if you know how, and there's issues with things like bump-stocks, but you can't just walk into a store that sells guns and buy the equivalent of the assault rifle in TC core. No amount of cash is going to let you walk into a store and buy something they can't even legally keep in stock.</div> </div> </div> </div>One more reason for a Assault Rifle being so expensive...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:07:58-07:00","id":1451306,"title":"","content":"So assuming a character is some kind of mercenary or something, how do they get an assault rifle? How do poor people get knives?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:54:53-07:00","id":1451315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451306#post1451306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So assuming a character is some kind of mercenary or something, how do they get an assault rifle? How do poor people get knives?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're a mercenary, you probably have an applicable Role or Society Path. You get your gun as starting equipment for that path. If you need a new gun during play, you use your Path contact to get one.<br /> <br /> If you're poor, you likely have a path related to your financial status. If any of your paths have a criminal component, you can start with a cheap weapon or get one via a contact. Also, anyone can afford a crap knife since they're effectively free. Take the core book's example knife and remove most of the tags, thereby giving you a free shiv.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:14:14-07:00","id":1451319,"title":"","content":"Where in the rules does it talk about Paths granting starting equipment? It seems like the rules don't say you start with a cheap weapon, you get a weapon with a number of additional tags equal to your Wealth. And if you do acquire a gun during play, given that each weapon is unique, wouldn't it still be bound by the Weapon Design rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:22:45-07:00","id":1451348,"title":"","content":"Paths specifically guiding starting equipment is on page 36 of TC core. Getting equipment through Paths is on page 40 via the Access Connection.<br /> <br /> The Wealth Edge specifies that Wealth represents extra disposable income, not the money necessary for your basic needs (and that you can take Complications if you don't have enough Wealth to buy something outright).<br /> <br /> While any weapon is theoretically bound by the weapon design rules, a character isn't bound by them for a weapon they didn't buy. If the PCs take down a rich mobster and find a cache of high end weapons, the weapons don't magically become worse because they don't have a mob boss's Wealth (which would be a GM fiat decision anyway since Wealth is a PC mechanic not a NPC one). So if the mob boss is rich enough to qualify as Wealth 5, that weapon cache having some weapons with 6 points worth of tags in them that the PCs without Wealth 5 take? Completely legit.<br /> <br /> I'm really not sure why people want to fight the game on this. Trinity isn't a gritty survival horror game where you need to carefully shepherd equipment as a vital resource. TC is an action adventure romp. Characters have the basic tools of their trade so they can go have cool adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:31:11-07:00","id":1451350,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I find Storypath very liberating, but there are people out there who read the rules as very restrictive and if it isn't allowed in the rules, it's just not allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T12:06:32-07:00","id":1451364,"title":"","content":"I think the trick to starting a game with appropriate equipment from your paths is to assume you have reasonable possessions for those paths without going full munchkin, since that'll annoy the storyguide.<br /> <br /> Are you an international jewel thief? You've got a high end (but not top tier) B&amp;E kit.<br /> <br /> Are you a getaway driver? You start with a fast car, but not some sort of super Wealth 5 car. If you want the Wealth 5 car, that is an in-game goal.<br /> <br /> Are you a fighter pilot? You have a light civilian or antique military aircraft you take out for a spin on the weekends, but it won't have functional weapons unless you add them in-game.<br /> <br /> Are you a computer hacker? You've got an expensive new PC with some illegal hacking programs installed, but you're not starting with your own private supercomputer (supercomputer access is gained on a per case basis via your contacts).<br /> <br /> Are you a PC? (I'll assume the answer is yes). You start with at least one appropriate weapon/armor option; hackers/medics should get a taser or holdout pistol and bulletproof vest, while combat oriented party members likely carry several heavier weapons and better armor. These probably won't be top of the line unless they expend points on appropriate edges, since getting more/better equipment should be a campaign subgoal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T12:53:58-07:00","id":1451370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451348#post1451348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While any weapon is theoretically bound by the weapon design rules, a character isn't bound by them for a weapon they didn't buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And where does it say that? Like, I'm not trying to be difficult, but I'm not reading the Wealth rules, I'm reading the Weapon rules. That is what it says. It doesn't offer any provisions for a weapon having any other stats. And all page 36 says is literally &quot;Connected to those decisions and experiences are people \u2014 coworkers, friends, followers, family \u2014 and resources \u2014 lab space, heavy equipment, research archives \u2014 that each character can still access.&quot; It doesn't say anything about starting with a gun. The access rules don't really say anything about the value of an item. If you do get &quot;a gun&quot; there is nothing in the rules to suggest whats its stats should be except Weapon Design, which states each and every weapon you own gains tags based on your Wealth.<br /> <br /> I'm hearing a lot of reasonable suggestions on how to hand out equipment, but none of it seems to have anything to do with the rulebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> getting more/better equipment should be a campaign subgoal. </div> </div> </div>It's not even clear that frees you from the tyranny of the Wealth rules, but anyway, no, a beginning adventurer starting with a run-of-the-mill pistol isn't really a campaign subgoal.<br /> <br /> Can someone explain to me how the Weapon Design rules aren't simply broken?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T13:05:57-07:00","id":1451371,"title":"","content":"If you need a rules-based excuse for people to start with the stuff their paths would give them access to, go with &quot;When to Roll Dice&quot; on page 69 of the core book. An active member of the military should not have any problem getting ahold of their service weapon. There's no need to roll for that. That's an example of a path granting someone starting equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T13:21:21-07:00","id":1451374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451370#post1451370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not even clear that frees you from the tyranny of the Wealth rules, but anyway, no, a beginning adventurer starting with a run-of-the-mill pistol isn't really a campaign subgoal.<br /> <br /> Can someone explain to me how the Weapon Design rules aren't simply broken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Wealth rules aren't for run-of-the-mill items. That example weapon table? Those are custom designed weapons. (That's based off of the Weapon Creation paragraph on page 123.)<br /> <br /> If you want to build a run-of-the-mill pistol using the weapon creation rules, take the the default weapon of Enhancement 1, Close range, and 1 point of weapon tag. Choose Ranged (short) as the extra tag, you now have a pistol. It cots 0 Wealth, and there is nothing special about it. A knife is done similarly with the Grapple or Piercing tag instead of Ranged. Anything better than that takes Wealth, which makes sense, since with Wealth 0 you're basically living hand to mouth.<br /> <br /> But honestly, if you're approaching the Wealth rules as something tyrannical, you're approaching this game in the wrong way. If you just cannot wrap your head around requiring even a basic amount of disposable income to buy a shotgun (because it should have the Spread tag along with Ranged, which would require 1 Wealth,) then give an extra tag for free or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T13:54:01-07:00","id":1451379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451371#post1451371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you need a rules-based excuse for people to start with the stuff their paths would give them access to, go with &quot;When to Roll Dice&quot; on page 69 of the core book. An active member of the military should not have any problem getting ahold of their service weapon. There's no need to roll for that. That's an example of a path granting someone starting equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I checked, and there is nothing in that section about equipment at all. Also, &quot;has a gun&quot; isn't a roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451364#post1451364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the trick to starting a game with appropriate equipment from your paths is to assume you have reasonable possessions for those paths without going full munchkin, since that'll annoy the storyguide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yeah, I am getting the impression that the best way to deal with the rules for Weapon Design is to ignore them.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any further thoughts beyond &quot;don't use the rules&quot; and &quot;if you thought you were going to use the rules, do you even game bro?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","user":"pawsplay","date":". 06-08-2021, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T14:23:18-07:00","id":1451386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451379#post1451379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I checked, and there is nothing in that section about equipment at all. Also, &quot;has a gun&quot; isn't a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but using your path to acquire one can be a roll. I guess I needed to be more explicit:<br /> <br /> 1. The Mercenary path gives them a contact or community which could provide them with a weapon with a roll.<br /> <br /> 2. Since they've had the path for some amount of time, it's reasonable to assume they've had time to acquire a weapon via their path before the game starts.<br /> <br /> 3. Don't roll, just let them have the weapon, no matter what their wealth is. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, yeah, I am getting the impression that the best way to deal with the rules for Weapon Design is to ignore them.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any further thoughts beyond &quot;don't use the rules&quot; and &quot;if you thought you were going to use the rules, do you even game bro?&quot; </div> </div> </div>You mean besides explaining how to start with a knife as a Wealth 0 person? Or how to start with an assault rifle as a mercenary? Those can both be done within the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T14:32:36-07:00","id":1451387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451386#post1451386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but using your path to acquire one can be a roll. I guess I needed to be more explicit:<br /> <br /> 1. The Mercenary path gives them a contact or community which could provide them with a weapon with a roll.<br /> <br /> 2. Since they've had the path for some amount of time, it's reasonable to assume they've had time to acquire a weapon via their path before the game starts.<br /> <br /> 3. Don't roll, just let them have the weapon, no matter what their wealth is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds very reasonable. And completely ignores what the rules say about starting with a weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You mean besides explaining how to start with a knife as a Wealth 0 person? Or how to start with an assault rifle as a mercenary? Those can both be done within the rules. </div> </div> </div>I mean, i get it, you can start as a mercenary with a pea-shooter that you say is an assault rifle, whereas the bad guys you fight have assault rifles only a multi-billionaire can afford. Or you ignore the rules as written entirely, that works, too.<br /> <br /> Let me rephrase. Is there any way, going by the rules in the book and not assuming made-up die rolls which you then ignore, with unknown difficulties because weapons don't have a cost, just Tags, for paramilitary or criminal PCs to start with typical weapons, without requiring two or more dots of Wealth? Is there anything in the rules that suggests you can sidestep the Wealth and Weapon Design Rules, or do we just throw our hands up in the air and not use those rules at all, instead just relying on vague language about connections to equip characters, with no particular parameters on what characters get strong equipment or not?<br /> <br /> Are the weapons rules just superfluous? Can I just roll Aim + Dexterity with no Enhancements and just say I'm using an assault rifle of an unremarkable description?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T14:47:43-07:00","id":1451391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451370#post1451370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I'm not trying to be difficult,....</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment I am 99.99% convinced you are, in fact, being difficult on purpose, and there's no point in trying to explain the rules to you, since you want the rules to be broken for whatever reasons you want them to be broken instead of any good faith effort to understand the rules.<br /> <br /> If I'm wrong, feel free to actually take a stab at convincing me but the last few posts all scream, &quot;I am here for the sole purpose of ranting about how bad the rules are and nothing anyone says will dissuade me.&quot; Since, you know, you're clearing ignoring the rules as they're printed and taking them as a whole, and instead are trying to have the different aspects of this &quot;fight&quot; each other in some vain attempt to demonstrate things don't work as intended if you just follow what the rules suggest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T16:38:43-07:00","id":1451404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451370#post1451370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not even clear that frees you from the tyranny of the Wealth rules, but anyway, no, a beginning adventurer starting with a run-of-the-mill pistol isn't really a campaign subgoal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're absolutely right that a character starting the game with a pistol isn't a campaign subgoal. That'd be stupid. That also isn't at all what I wrote in my post that you were quoting. It is in fact the exact opposite of what I wrote.<br /> <br /> Based on what I ACTUALLY wrote, a character without the Wealth Edge and an appropriate Path can start the game with a tricked out street racer from the original The Fast and The Furious movie, a small personal airplane, or a top of the line commercially available computer, but probably can't justify owning a car from Fate of the Furious, a modern fighter jet, or a supercomputer. Getting those options would be campaign subgoals; starting equipment is stuff you have because it is assumed you to have it.<br /> <br /> You seem to be completely misinterpreting the intent of the Wealth Edge. Edges in general are meant to be interesting/convenient shortcuts to getting what you want. The Wealth Edge in particular is mostly a way to throw money at problems until they go away.<br /> <br /> Need to get to Paris to stop your nemesis from enacting his diabolical plot? You could roleplay wheedling a favor out of someone, or you could just throw money at the problem and buy airline tickets for the entire party.<br /> <br /> Your old car got shot up and you need a new one NOW? You could roleplay getting a replacement, or you could just throw money at someone until they give you their car.<br /> <br /> The Wealth Edge isn't needed to do anything in the game, it is only a shortcut that lets you skip the boring stuff. The only interaction between Wealth and weapons is if you desperately need a weapon you can't get otherwise and decide to just throw money at a legal or illegal weapon seller to get one NOW.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, i get it, you can start as a mercenary with a pea-shooter that you say is an assault rifle, whereas the bad guys you fight have assault rifles only a multi-billionaire can afford. Or you ignore the rules as written entirely, that works, too. </div> </div> </div>Not even close. If your mercenary character wants to start out with a decent assault rifle (or even a small personal arsenal), that is completely okay, since an experienced mercenary is assumed to have lots of weapons. He just probably doesn't start with the absolute best cutting edge military grade weapons in the world unless he's currently in an elite military unit. But you know what? Neither do the typical faceless security forces he fights. I even said that outright one single sentence before the part of my post you quoted:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You start with at least one appropriate weapon/armor option; hackers/medics should get a taser or holdout pistol and bulletproof vest, while <b><u>combat oriented party members likely carry several heavier weapons</u></b> and better armor. </div> </div> </div>Do you honestly think someone with zero Wealth starts out naked and homeless? You have those things and more; Wealth just justifies starting with a lot of other stuff as well. A Wealth 0 mercenary may have a crap car and crap apartment, but still has decent personal armor and more good quality weapons than he can carry at once, since these are a requirement for his job. A Wealth 5 mercenary has that arsenal plus a mansion and maybe even a private jet. If you're poor, you have stuff related to meeting your minimum physical needs plus meeting the expectations of your Paths. If you're rich, you're assumed to have whatever you need for your Paths, plus a bunch of other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T22:08:56-07:00","id":1451414,"title":"","content":"Again, I'm not here to talk about the Wealth edge specifically or what Wealth is for. I'm just trying to address how to gear up an armed beginning character. The only rules I am aware of are under Weapon Design, under Weapons (not under a section about Wealth). The two key points I'm struggling with are:<br /> 1) How do I implement the rules as written?<br /> 2) What is the intent? Since each weapon is unique, do you even need a &quot;weapon&quot; to attack, or is it a special trait (almost like a character, as the rules say) that just consists of a series of tags? If a weapon is just a customized group of tags, with no relationship to a diagetic, generic weapon, why is it so closely tied to Wealth?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you honestly think someone with zero Wealth starts out naked and homeless? </div> </div> </div>No, but I think, according to the core rulebook, they don't start off with a weapon with two or more positive tags. So, the itinerant big game hunter has a rifle with no tags at all other than Ranged (Long). His rifle isn't even Two-Handed.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about this, and it seems like it might make sense if there were a house rule or maybe an Edge that a weapon can have extra tags equal to the higher of your Wealth or the relevant Skill. Even if she's not rich, the skilled archer could have a compound bow with a bunch of tags. It's not a super bow, it's just the best of all possible bows for our skilled archer. I am just a little wary of double-dipping (getting both the dots in Skill and the tags) so maybe an Edge is a better way of going.<br /> <br /> But I don't know how to reconcile that in a world where an assault rifle is just one good Connections roll away. That doesn't seem very fair to the person who burned an Edge on better weapons. And if you can use your Connections to get weaponry, maybe that should be the basis instead of Wealth in the first place. Maybe buying weapons should be a secondary, less optimal way to get weapons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T01:59:55-07:00","id":1451423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451414#post1451414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) How do I implement the rules as written?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use paths, let characters take what is appropriate to their paths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) What is the intent? </div> </div> </div>Use paths, let characters take what is appropriate to their paths. <br /> <br /> *And*, when you ask the forum for answers, assume the people taking the time to reply are doing so in good faith, and then stop arguing in what appears to be increasingly bad faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T08:45:28-07:00","id":1451445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451423#post1451423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Use paths, let characters take what is appropriate to their paths.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Use paths, let characters take what is appropriate to their paths.<br /> <br /> *And*, when you ask the forum for answers, assume the people taking the time to reply are doing so in good faith, and then stop arguing in what appears to be increasingly bad faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you're a dev. Maybe you can help me understand better.<br /> <br /> 1) Why does the Weapon Design section of the Weapon section say you get one additional tag per dot of Wealth? What is that rule for, and when is it invoked?<br /> <br /> 2) I've been chewing on the book for a while now, but I just joined the forums a few days ago. If I were living on a desert island, reading this book, how would I glean &quot;Paths&quot; is the answer to starting adventuring equipment? Is there any guidance beyond &quot;ask the Story Guide?&quot; Can a character borrowing or acquiring equipment from a Path in fact ignore the Weapon Design rules, including the limit on the number of tags?<br /> <br /> 3) If I make an Access check, is there a good way to set the difficulty? Does a weapon's Wealth rating affect the difficulty? If I'm using Access to acquire a weapon, do I still have the choice of customizing the tags, and if so, does the resulting Wealth rating affect the difficulty? For instance, could I say, I just want an &quot;assault rifle&quot; that is just a weapon with the Range tag. Is that easier to acquire?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:27:33-07:00","id":1451470,"title":"","content":"Not Bunyip obviously, but I'll take another swing at things:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451445#post1451445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Why does the Weapon Design section of the Weapon section say you get one additional tag per dot of Wealth?</div> </div> </div> </div>To determine how the specialized combat equipment interacts with Wealth as combat equipment has extra details normal gear doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is that rule for, and when is it invoked? </div> </div> </div>When a character wants to buy something outright and not have the strings attached that come with using Paths or taking out loans to get something.<br /> <br /> If your playing a cop, and you get a pistol, body armor, and a car that are all better than your Wealth rating would allow from your Role Path, that equipment doesn't belong to you, it belongs to the police department. If you don't fulfill your obligations or you over tap your Path for favors, you run the risk of having your access to those things taken away (such as being put on desk duty pending internal review of your activities).<br /> <br /> If you've used Wealth to buy some personal gear as well, it's yours. It's subject to the plot of course, but no organization is going to come knocking for it back, or want you to repay the &quot;kindness&quot; of getting it for you. You don't have a loan hanging over your head the next time you need to get something fast that you can't afford outright. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I were living on a desert island, reading this book, how would I glean &quot;Paths&quot; is the answer to starting adventuring equipment? </div> </div> </div>Page 36, as previously noted, that part that's in the character creation section and says that Paths represent resources your character has access to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any guidance beyond &quot;ask the Story Guide?&quot; </div> </div> </div>When creating your Path, communicate your intentions to the SG so they know what you're after, and then accept SG input on adjusting it for the tone of the specific game you're going to be in.<br /> <br /> Players design their characters' Paths. the SG helps bring them to life and make sure they're going to be fun in play. Page 132 is important to keep in mind here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a character borrowing or acquiring equipment from a Path in fact ignore the Weapon Design rules, including the limit on the number of tags? </div> </div> </div>They are not bound by their Wealth dots in terms of how many tags the equipment they get has, but the weapons still have to make sense with those rules as adjudicated by the SG based on how the player defined their Path. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I make an Access check, is there a good way to set the difficulty? </div> </div> </div>Access checks don't have a default difficulty. The more successes you roll the better equipment you can get (which is another benefit of Wealth, there's no roll to risk). Your Path rating is temporarily reduced if you keep tapping it, leaving you with less dice to roll, and if you skimp on your obligations or get suspended, you face extra complications to the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a weapon's Wealth rating affect the difficulty? </div> </div> </div>No, but it's not a bad guide for SGs to use to think up what a successful access check comes up with since weapons are more complex than what level of enhancement they grant like most equipment. Getting 1 success to ask for a gun isn't going to get you as impressive a gun as rolling 3 successes, so Wealth makes sense as a metric for what that means. You can ask your Path connections for whatever you want, but that doesn't mean they're going to have that exact thing &quot;in stock.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I'm using Access to acquire a weapon, do I still have the choice of customizing the tags... </div> </div> </div>Again, the access roll has no difficulty and how well you roll on it is what matters. The better you roll, the closer to what you want your connections should be able to get you (either more tags, or specific tags).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T13:38:19-07:00","id":1451482,"title":"","content":"Everyone in the thread who are acting like trinity tags arent presented poorly is being obtuse. I love the system concept but its poorly explained. The very first weapon in the game, the assualt rifle, has too many tags for even the wealthiest man in the world to own without having intrinsic scale. Weapons were obviously meant to have a scale yet that is one sentence worth. I would recommend op consider looking at the scale table to for tags in addition to wealth but that still doesnt help with what a character should be able to start with. So ask the ST","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T14:03:20-07:00","id":1451487,"title":"","content":"The presentation, and even the valuation, of tags isn't really relevant to the question of &quot;what can I start with?&quot; To which the answer remains, &quot;whatever makes sense for you Paths.&quot; Scale is another non sequitur here, as Scale is something everything has; it's just if Scale is relevant or not to a situation (that is, if things are operating on different Scales or not).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T14:19:02-07:00","id":1451489,"title":"","content":"No where is that stated. The literal rules state differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T14:54:32-07:00","id":1451496,"title":"","content":"And remember scale adds tags. But no where does it mention if you can or cant start with weapons at any scale. <br /> <br /> So again, the book gives you an interesting system but then doesnt have sensible examples. This is the worst part of the 2 books Ive read, core and aberrant. I dont like aeon and dont care to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T15:23:12-07:00","id":1451504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451489#post1451489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No where is that stated. The literal rules state differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>The literal rules for creating a character say that your Paths determine what resources you have access to, as has been cited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451496#post1451496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And remember scale adds tags.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I called it a non-sequitur. You're not wrong that how Scale and tags interact is off as-written, but it doesn't change that Paths are what determines what you have access to at creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But no where does it mention if you can or cant start with weapons at any scale. </div> </div> </div>If I make a character that drives a tank, I have access to weapons that would give me significant scale bonuses against people not in military combat vehicles. If I make the lead singer in a band? I don't.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what's hard or confusing about that.<br /> <br /> The problem with scale is that the books don't usually have you directly assign scale to things, because scale was envisioned as a relative number rather than an absolute one. Adding tags with scale either means weapon tags change as scale changes (which isn't necessarily bad, an assault rifle loosing tags when attacking an armored train, but gaining them against a mouse would make sense even if scale is supposed to abstract away all that), or weapons, armor, and vehicles need to be assigned scale.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't matter to what equipment you can start with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T02:23:43-07:00","id":1451530,"title":"","content":"Must note it down: the best path to wealth in Trinity is having a knife factory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T11:06:45-07:00","id":1451554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451504#post1451504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The literal rules for creating a character say that your Paths determine what resources you have access to, as has been cited.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I called it a non-sequitur. You're not wrong that how Scale and tags interact is off as-written, but it doesn't change that Paths are what determines what you have access to at creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I make a character that drives a tank, I have access to weapons that would give me significant scale bonuses against people not in military combat vehicles. If I make the lead singer in a band? I don't.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what's hard or confusing about that.<br /> <br /> The problem with scale is that the books don't usually have you directly assign scale to things, because scale was envisioned as a relative number rather than an absolute one. Adding tags with scale either means weapon tags change as scale changes (which isn't necessarily bad, an assault rifle loosing tags when attacking an armored train, but gaining them against a mouse would make sense even if scale is supposed to abstract away all that), or weapons, armor, and vehicles need to be assigned scale.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't matter to what equipment you can start with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not confusing, its contradictory. Two different methods for creating starting gear and nothing noting how they are supposed to interact. Either wealth is necessary or completely useless. <br /> <br /> I enjoy the game and play bi weekly, but acting like the equipment (or crafting) system is perfect is not how I find joy. The Assault Rifle for instance, the very first weapon listed, is impossible to construct with the rules given.<br /> <br /> So you know that the Power scale of a weapon doesnt change depending on the target right? That is what Durability scale is for. Power has a beautiful breakdown of what roughly each scale level corrosponds to. 1- punches 2- pistols 3- assualt rifles You need numbers to find a relative difference as well as to determine what tags a weapon has.<br /> <br /> Your idea of changing tags isnt supported by the book and seems like a useless time sink to implement in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T11:17:06-07:00","id":1451555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451554#post1451554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its not confusing, its contradictory. Two different methods for creating starting gear and nothing noting how they are supposed to interact. Either wealth is necessary or completely useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says they need to interact? They can both provide starting equipment. Paths cover things you SHOULD have, and Wealth covers things you COULD have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T14:51:47-07:00","id":1451580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451554#post1451554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not confusing, its contradictory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please cite a passage that says you use Wealth to determine starting equipment, and then you can call it a contradiction. Wealth is only mentioned once in character creation: in the example of Path selection where the player decides to take the Edge for one of their Paths. The rules for Wealth in the Edge section do not say it governs starting gear (in fact, it says that with or without Wealth you're presumed to have the basic gear of your lifestyle). The rules for weapons, armor, and vehicles do not say they are used in character creation.<br /> <br /> So you're going to have to cite an actual contradiction in the rules here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either wealth is necessary or completely useless. </div> </div> </div>No... as I've detailed previously there are lots of benefits to using Wealth to get things over relying on Paths (plus other little things like Weath capping how much superscience a non-Inspired character can have to fund maintaining such wondrous devices). Wealth lets you get what you want, as you want it, without all of the consequences that come from going through Paths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I enjoy the game and play bi weekly, but acting like the equipment (or crafting) system is perfect is not how I find joy. </div> </div> </div>Nobody's saying the system is perfect, but valid complaints about one part of the system don't inherently mean complaints about another part of the system are valid. You can be right about one part of the game being flawed and be wrong about a different part of the game being flawed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your idea of changing tags isnt supported by the book and seems like a useless time sink to implement in a game. </div> </div> </div>Yeah... that's why it's an &quot;or&quot; statement. The idea of the total construct of the paragraph in question is that you really do need to assign weapons/etc. Scale as a value with how the rules are constructed even though the game doesn't really address that in a thorough way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T16:14:08-07:00","id":1451588,"title":"","content":"Eh I see two rule sets operating in the same space without even an idea of how they should interact as very poor design. I\u2019ll say the following in purpose of further discourse rather than any real belief. <br /> You may be right in very technical sense But if you are, then rules are contradictory in spirit instead. <br /> The weapon rules claim they are for individuals characterize interesting weapons. But then trying to use the system ends up with the ST creating all the cool weapons. Because they are the high wealth npc. They are blacksmith/Q. So if you get path equipment your character has no control over what that means. <br /> <br /> Not to mention you ignoring the points in the rest of my post<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T16:58:47-07:00","id":1451594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451588#post1451588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh I see two rule sets operating in the same space without even an idea of how they should interact as very poor design.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the rules operate in the same space: the game.<br /> <br /> Your logic, taken to the extreme, means all RPGs are purely poor design, because &quot;same space&quot; is a vague and arbitrary criteria. Only the most abstract systems where everything is resolved using a single mechanic can possibly avoid having more than one way to accomplish something in the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You may be right in very technical sense But if you are, then rules are contradictory in spirit instead. </div> </div> </div>Nope. Addressed more than sufficiently already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then trying to use the system ends up with the ST creating all the cool weapons. </div> </div> </div>Um no? Only getting access to weapons with Paths would be up to the SG to create; and even then the SG is bound by how the player defines their Paths and the access connection roll not just their own fiat. Weapons bought with Wealth, made with crafting, etc. are what the player defines.<br /> <br /> The Storypath system stresses that it is a collaborative game where the SG and players work together and the SG should look at places to share their responsibilities. A SG is not failing to follow the letter of the rules, and the spirit of the rules, to respond to an access connection roll with, &quot;you get a weapon with X tags based on that roll, feel free to assign them as makes sense to what you were asking for.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention you ignoring the points in the rest of my post </div> </div> </div>The majority of your points so far seem to be, &quot;there's a spelling mistake on p. XX, therefore I don't have to prove anything I say about how weapons work.&quot; Even then, I have no idea what you think wasn't actually addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T19:18:56-07:00","id":1451601,"title":"","content":"I honestly don\u2019t understand the confusion in bringing the two together. Paths describe who you are and what you do. Having items suitable for those Paths is straight forward. And Wealth is for all the other things you might want, if you can afford them.<br /> <br /> Look at the movie Bad Boys. (It\u2019s just the example that springs to mind.) Will Smith\u2019s character - Mike Lowry - is a cop. As a cop, you expect him to have a badge, a gun (or more - it\u2019s the US), probably handcuffs, and access to the precinct. The character also has a Porsche. That\u2019s not exactly police issue and isn\u2019t something I\u2019d allow for the character as SG. But Mike Lowry\u2019s background is that his family died and left him money. He has Wealth and he used that to justify the fancy sports car that he uses for police work. (Hey, it\u2019s an action movie where rule of cool applies, same for Trinity Continuum.) Meanwhile, his partner, Marcus, is also a cop. He has badge, gun, and access, but no sports car. He has a wife and children, and as a cop presumably has stable enough income to handle the bills and mortgage. He doesn\u2019t need Wealth for these things, but he doesn\u2019t have spare cash to drop on frivolous things either.<br /> <br /> If the character\u2019s a soldier, they have uniform, fatigues, and whatever gear is appropriate to the mission. If they\u2019re a VARG pilot, or a jet fighter pilot, they have access to those things, too. But the banker working on Wall Street doesn\u2019t have a gun or an assault rifle, or a fighter jet. None of those things are appropriate to his Paths. But he probably has a ton of Wealth. If he has enough and he wants to buy those things, he can do so. (Though they\u2019re restricted access or illegal, so SG may say no, or use them as sources of story drama.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T20:37:23-07:00","id":1451607,"title":"","content":"Ok then Bunyip, is a pistol scale 2 when building a weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T01:35:31-07:00","id":1451620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451580#post1451580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please cite a passage that says you use Wealth to determine starting equipment, and then you can call it a contradiction</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, the Weapon Design rules, under Weapons, is the place that states what tags your equipment can have. Notably, these rules are not even bounded by such things as &quot;starting equipment&quot; or &quot;acquiring resources in play through Access.&quot; So your requirement is irrelevant. The king rules here are the rules under Weapons. No other rule in the game, as best I can determine, modifies, overrides, comments on, or nullifies those rules. They aren't rules of Wealth. They are the very rules of weapons themselves.<br /> <br /> Further, the idea of Paths granting equipment is based on several spurious assumptions. Sure, a cop gets their gun and badge from an allegiance. But what kind of gun? Going by the rulebook, it is stated plainly that the tags of that gun depend on the cop's Wealth. There is no rule anywhere modifying that. And what if your background is being a criminal? You don't get a semi-automatic pistol by being assigned by it an agency. You own it, even though, like most criminals, you don't have considerable personal wealth.<br /> <br /> Further, further, the Weapons rules specify that each weapon has unique attributes. The weapon table is identified as a table of example weapons. If you assume you just have stuff based on your paths, you are now treating a table of example, custome-designed weapons as though it were a standard equipment table, like those found in other role-playing games, and then handing them out arbitrarily based on a character's background story. The weapons, at that point, are not connected to any dots in anything, and have arbitrary statistics.<br /> <br /> I'm very discouraged at this point. Even after comments by devs, it's not clear what weapons are. Let me lay out three options:<br /> <br /> 1) In a game like Cortex, weapons aren't real. You might have a trait like Glock d8, but that doesn't mean that other characters don't have Glocks. That's just the benefit your Glock gives to you. NPC mobs don't have Glocks at all in that sense. Other characters might shoot a Glock, but they don't have a Glock trait. They might just roll their Soldier d8 trait or their Marksmanship or whatever, but a gun doesn't have any traits at all unless you make it a signature piece of equipment or create it during play as a Resource. In Trinity terms, any character could just roll Aim + Dexterity at any time and declare they are firing a gun. AND I DON'T KNOW WHETHER THIS IS TRUE IN TRINITY FROM READING THE RULES.<br /> <br /> 2) In a game like Savage Worlds, weapons are real. Every weapon has a cost in dollars, a damage die, a range, et cetera. You acquire a gun out of your starting equipment allowance, and all guns of the same type you find in the game have the same statistics. As written, the rules seem to suggest this is not how Trinity works.<br /> <br /> 3) In a game like M&amp;M, or Champions, there are charts of standardized weapons. There is a light pistol, and all light pistols wielded by common criminals have these statistics, unless the GM gives the guns different statistics. But your gun might have any statistics you give it, using example weapons only for inspiration. The GM might ask, &quot;Why does your light pistol have Damage 6?&quot; and this is a fair question, but there's nothing in the game from forbidding it. To me, this is how Trinity appears to be written, or at least what the book implies to me. Weapons are somewhat &quot;real&quot; but your weapon is a customized trait that does whatever you say it does.<br /> <br /> If we assume option 1 is the case for Trinity, that solves a lot of problems. Any given melee weapon needs maybe one tag for how it wielded (Close, Two-Handed), and any given ranged weapon really just needs a Range. But you could just say, &quot;I shoot a gun&quot; (Aim + Dexterity) and gain no Enhancement, while also incurring no Range penalties or otherwise dealing with the description of the gun. This works just like someone using Larceny and stating they are using lockpicks, normal un-enhanced lockpicks. The main problem, as I noted above, is that this creates an arbitrary relationship between Wealth and firepower. A commando and a millionaire might both have a knife, and purely because of how Weapon Design works, the millionaire's knife is much, much better.<br /> <br /> Bunyip seems to suggest Paths can just hand out appropriate equipment. Apart from being, you know, not in the rules (other than saying, ok, yeah, characters have resources), this relies on Option 2, weapons are real. Otherwise, the free weapons you do or don't get, don't have any statistics. Because Option 3 suggests the example weapons are, just that, examples, and don't really traits you can rely on because of your character. To me, Bunyip's suggestion does not seem relevant to the Trinity Continuum core rulebook. Bunyip's suggestion amounts to, essentially, we have no idea what tags someone's weapon has, based on anything, the Story Guide just sort of approves or doesn't approve weapons with an arbitrary number of tags. During play, you can use Access to access other weapons, using a non-predetermined difficulty, to acquire other weapons with an arbitrary and undetermined number of tags. Because there is nowhere in the book that says, &quot;This is what the capability of a Rifle is.&quot; A Rifle has whatever capabilities it has, according to the tags you assign it.<br /> <br /> Almost all the advice I'm getting that has any utility suggests that people are handling weapons as they are handled in other games, and now how they are handled in TC. It's not &quot;bad&quot; advice, it's just not advice for a game in which Weapon Design is a heading nestled under Weapons, and which says you custom design weapons by assigning them a number of tags based on your Wealth, and in which page 36 specifies, in a vague sort of way, that Paths provide Resources, but only providing rules for asking for things during play and then without any suggestion of standard difficulties.<br /> <br /> In my view, this topic requires substantial clarification and/or errata for TC to be usable &quot;out of the box&quot; without leaving GMs and players adrift.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note that I did not create this topic, I found it while searching the forums trying to figure out how this stuff is supposed to work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","user":"pawsplay","date":". 06-11-2021, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T03:49:37-07:00","id":1451629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451620#post1451620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, the Weapon Design rules, under Weapons, is the place that states what tags your equipment can have.</div> </div> </div> </div>It never says to use it for character creation.<br /> <br /> Let's try something different:<br /> <br /> How good of a computer (rating by the Enhancement it gives) do you think a character can start with? Computers, not being weapons, armor, or a vehicle, doesn't have tags, and isn't impacted by the design rules, so your issues with those rules don't impact this decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Further, the idea of Paths granting equipment is based on several spurious assumptions. </div> </div> </div>No, it's based on the text literally saying Paths can get you access to equipment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You own it, even though, like most criminals, you don't have considerable personal wealth. </div> </div> </div>Even if you want to ignore Paths as a viable way to get a gun with more than the default one tag, the Wealth rules let you acquire items worth more Wealth than you have at the cost on complications arising from how you went about doing that. If your criminal doesn't have a lot of disposable money from their crimes, but wants a gun they can't just pay out of pocket for, they get one from a criminal with better connections, and owe that other criminal a favor.<br /> <br /> Or do you think the rules are saying that if you use the Wealth rules to by a mansion despite being Wealth 0 and taking the complications for it lets you have a mansion, but if you buy a fancy gun the same way, it reverts to a one tag weapon at some point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you assume you just have stuff based on your paths, you are now treating a table of example, custome-designed weapons as though it were a standard equipment table,... </div> </div> </div>No, Path based equipment is not restricted to the example table. I already went over this for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The weapons, at that point, are not connected to any dots in anything, and have arbitrary statistics. </div> </div> </div>They're &quot;connected&quot; to your path (which has a rating), and all weapons in all RPGs have arbitrary statistics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm very discouraged at this point. </div> </div> </div>You're not really doing much to change the perception that you never wanted anything other than to be discouraged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me lay out three options: </div> </div> </div>TC doesn't slot into any of these; maybe that's the problem here?<br /> <br /> Weapons, in TC, are a fourth option the lives somewhere between option #1 and #2. Weapons are &quot;real&quot; not just character traits, however the game assumes that the PCs will start with/acquire/build/etc. unique and personalized equipment for themselves and applies rules to govern doing that which are based on the character instead of the &quot;reality&quot; of the weapon.<br /> <br /> TC also has strong PC/NPC asymmetry. Default NPCs work strictly like option #1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apart from being, you know, not in the rules (other than saying, ok, yeah, characters have resources), </div> </div> </div>&quot;As long as you ignore the rules that says this is the rules, this isn't the rules,&quot; is one hell of a set of mental gymnastics. Paths literally have rules for gained equipment. That is the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....Resources, but only providing rules for asking for things during play and then without any suggestion of standard difficulties. </div> </div> </div>I explained how the Access rules work. It is not &quot;beg your SG,&quot; since you can use Path connections whenever you want as long as it makes sense for the timing, and it doesn't suggest &quot;standard difficulties&quot; because the results are based on how well you roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my view, this topic requires substantial clarification and/or errata for TC to be usable &quot;out of the box&quot; without leaving GMs and players adrift. </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you think we're shocked that, predictably, you ended where you started because you're not actually listening to the explanations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that I did not create this topic, I found it while searching the forums trying to figure out how this stuff is supposed to work. </div> </div> </div>Most of us are perfectly aware of that. We can, in fact, read a four page thread and usually separate different posters in our minds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T04:27:36-07:00","id":1451632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451607#post1451607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok then Bunyip, is a pistol scale 2 when building a weapon?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, no. A pistol is not scale 2, it\u2019s scale 1 as all the other personal weapons without the Heavy Weapon tag.<br /> <br /> If the idea is to have a high lethality in a gun fight (something real and not very action movie) a gun, and even a sword to that end, can be scale 2. What is the impact? First, you can cause 3 injuries with a single shot, what can put down many characters with a single shot, second, it will give enhancements that would make most of the armors useless (unless you give them scale too), as result it will make most fights end quick and the characters will have more injuries by their ends, and so I would say gun fights will be something most characters would avoid. Pretty much real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T05:38:07-07:00","id":1451642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451632#post1451632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By default, no. A pistol is not scale 2, it\u2019s scale 1 as all the other personal weapons without the Heavy Weapon tag.<br /> <br /> If the idea is to have a high lethality in a gun fight (something real and not very action movie) a gun, and even a sword to that end, can be scale 2. What is the impact? First, you can cause 3 injuries with a single shot, what can put down many characters with a single shot, second, it will give enhancements that would make most of the armors useless (unless you give them scale too), as result it will make most fights end quick and the characters will have more injuries by their ends, and so I would say gun fights will be something most characters would avoid. Pretty much real world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why are weapons listed on the power scale and a pistol is at 2? How do we craft a scale 3 weapon using the rules? <br /> What is a personal weapon? an anti personal weapon or something not jet mounted? <br /> So rocket launchers are scale 1, 2 with the heavy weapons tag? Why is scale mentioned in making weapon then?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to play aberrant so scale is incredibly important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T05:57:50-07:00","id":1451643,"title":"","content":"Starting characters can have a scale of 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T05:59:49-07:00","id":1451644,"title":"","content":"Aberrant specifically modifies the Scale system in ways that aren't intended to apply to the TC series in general. In Aberrant specifically, most firearms are going to be Scale 2, but so is most person armor.... which means they cancel out in play, but in Aberrant will start with more tags than in baseline TC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T06:02:27-07:00","id":1451645,"title":"","content":"Heavy do you have anything to support that? Because it says extension not revision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T06:22:29-07:00","id":1451648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451644#post1451644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aberrant specifically modifies the Scale system in ways that aren't intended to apply to the TC series in general. In Aberrant specifically, most firearms are going to be Scale 2, but so is most person armor.... which means they cancel out in play, but in Aberrant will start with more tags than in baseline TC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where is this stated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T08:23:39-07:00","id":1451668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451642#post1451642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why are weapons listed on the power scale and a pistol is at 2? How do we craft a scale 3 weapon using the rules?<br /> What is a personal weapon? an anti personal weapon or something not jet mounted?<br /> So rocket launchers are scale 1, 2 with the heavy weapons tag? Why is scale mentioned in making weapon then?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to play aberrant so scale is incredibly important.</div> </div> </div> </div>A regular TC Cora game deals mostly on Scale 1, because scale is not a daily thing regular people do. A grand master chess player have a skill trick to get scale on his \u201cplay chess\u201d rolls, for example, and even that guy can only achieve scale 2. Basically that is the idea of scale, one scale above is a LOT MORE.<br /> <br /> Personal weapon I use to describe weapons you carry on your self (assuming you are a regular weapon). A heavy machine gun is not a personal weapon, you can carry it around, but you can shoot it with your bare hands while holding it, the recoil and the weight is too much to do so, so it\u2019s a scale 2 weapon, like those side weapons a tank have or the machine guns installed on bunkers, for example. Those weapons when shot against people are not just deadly, they take body parts of, that is the idea of an scale 2 weapon damage on a scale 1 body.<br /> <br /> A RPG (the weapon, not the game) is an explosive and it is a bit weird on how it works, because it\u2019s cause damage on large areas, but not an absurd damage to parts, like a grenade, but launched at high speeds (possibly with some kind of armor piercing head to penetrate walls without exploding before). A Mortar is the same, it\u2019s a grenade launched in an area far from the launcher, possibly exploding in the air, if desired. As a general rule, explosives don\u2019t have scale rules, they just explode and follow the indirect damage rules, a \u201chigher scale\u201d explosive just have a higher DR and possibly a higher area of effect.<br /> <br /> Aberrant weaponry is not about regular weapon, it\u2019s Super Science, and it uses powers to increase the effectiveness of the equipment. A Super Tech pistol is not a gun you can find in real world, it\u2019s a hand cannon that can only exist due the fact a Nova developed some kind of material or technology that can cause this kind of damage, we are talking about bullets doing Mach 8, or firing singularities, or bullets the size of a fist traveling at bullet speed, if it\u2019s Physical damage, and so it can be what ever scale you can build them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T08:50:28-07:00","id":1451671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451629#post1451629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's based on the text literally saying Paths can get you access to equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say what equipment, and my question is, what equipment?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if you want to ignore Paths as a viable way to get a gun with more than the default one tag, the Wealth rules let you acquire items worth more Wealth than you have at the cost on complications arising from how you went about doing that. If your criminal doesn't have a lot of disposable money from their crimes, but wants a gun they can't just pay out of pocket for, they get one from a criminal with better connections, and owe that other criminal a favor. </div> </div> </div>And that's workable for when you want to acquire a new gun, and it's something that would reasonably be expensive. From my own personal experience, I know plenty of criminals who simply own a gun and have no dots in Wealth and don't particularly owe anyone for the gun. You are absolutely right, you CAN do that. What you CAN'T seem to be able to do is stat up a criminal who has a pistol tucked into their pants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or do you think the rules are saying that if you use the Wealth rules to by a mansion despite being Wealth 0 and taking the complications for it lets you have a mansion, but if you buy a fancy gun the same way, it reverts to a one tag weapon at some point? </div> </div> </div>Insofar as the rules say anything, that's what it looks like they say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, Path based equipment is not restricted to the example table. I already went over this for you. </div> </div> </div>Just saying something, &quot;going over it,&quot; isn't helpful. I'm looking for information, not just someone asserting something, then repeating it, then repeating it again, without actually giving me useful information. I don't know what you think you've said, but &quot;here's how Paths might give a starting character a gun of a certain calibre&quot; is definitely not one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're &quot;connected&quot; to your path (which has a rating), and all weapons in all RPGs have arbitrary statistics. </div> </div> </div>Wow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're not really doing much to change the perception that you never wanted anything other than to be discouraged. </div> </div> </div>You know, at no point have I attempted to perform a psychological analysis of you or your motivations, and I would like the same courtesy in return. What I have done so far is searched the web forums for answers, asked the same question on a FB group, then came back here and asked questions to try to fill in the gaps of my understanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> TC doesn't slot into any of these; maybe that's the problem here?<br /> <br /> Weapons, in TC, are a fourth option the lives somewhere between option #1 and #2. Weapons are &quot;real&quot; not just character traits, however the game assumes that the PCs will start with/acquire/build/etc. unique and personalized equipment for themselves and applies rules to govern doing that which are based on the character instead of the &quot;reality&quot; of the weapon. </div> </div> </div>That's really just #2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> TC also has strong PC/NPC asymmetry. Default NPCs work strictly like option #1. </div> </div> </div>And that's fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;As long as you ignore the rules that says this is the rules, this isn't the rules,&quot; is one hell of a set of mental gymnastics. Paths literally have rules for gained equipment. That is the rules.<br /> <br /> I explained how the Access rules work. It is not &quot;beg your SG,&quot; since you can use Path connections whenever you want as long as it makes sense for the timing, and it doesn't suggest &quot;standard difficulties&quot; because the results are based on how well you roll.<br /> </div> </div> </div>The rules are literally just &quot;you could roll for this.&quot; As opposed to the Weapon Design rules which are are strictly codified. Do you understand the problem I'm having? Because I feel like I'm having double vision here. It seems like it's just being repeatedly stated to ignore the Weapon Design rules, but still use the tags in that section, and how many, there are no rules. Do you mean something other than that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure you think we're shocked that, predictably, you ended where you started because you're not actually listening to the explanations. </div> </div> </div>Okay, rude. Maybe your explanations just suck and only make sense to people with your background of experiences. Or maybe your explanation seems to be to just ignore the most pertinent section of the rulebook, and beef up one of the vague-iest sections of the rulebook, and you don't understand why my brain violently rebels against what you seem to be saying because it's such a useless response.<br /> <br /> If the rule is supposed to be &quot;you have what your Paths suggest&quot; why aren't there two sentences supporting that in the rulebook? Why does the whole Weapon Design section of the rulebook contradict that? What is the purpose of the Weapon Design section if the rules you suggest, the Paths rules, give ZERO guidance on what and how many weapon tags the weapon you acquire should have?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T09:19:17-07:00","id":1451678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451671#post1451671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't say what equipment, and my question is, what equipment?</div> </div> </div> </div>It DOES say. It says &quot;The access connection is the equipment or specialized space (e.g., lab, darkroom, gym) related to the Path,&quot; pg. 40. It's part of every path. IT is any equipment related to the Path. You're not going to get a laundry list of items or &quot;characters should start with $10,000 worth of equipment per a dot of Wealth&quot;. You're going to start with the equipment it <b>makes sense</b> for your character to have based on their Paths. If your table can't figure out what equipment it makes sense for a member of the military, a hot shot lawyer, a gentleman thief, or an overly protective house husband to have at the beginning of the game, then you need to have a long talk with your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T09:28:12-07:00","id":1451680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451668#post1451668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A regular TC Cora game deals mostly on Scale 1, because scale is not a daily thing regular people do. A grand master chess player have a skill trick to get scale on his \u201cplay chess\u201d rolls, for example, and even that guy can only achieve scale 2. Basically that is the idea of scale, one scale above is a LOT MORE.<br /> <br /> Personal weapon I use to describe weapons you carry on your self (assuming you are a regular weapon). A heavy machine gun is not a personal weapon, you can carry it around, but you can shoot it with your bare hands while holding it, the recoil and the weight is too much to do so, so it\u2019s a scale 2 weapon, like those side weapons a tank have or the machine guns installed on bunkers, for example. Those weapons when shot against people are not just deadly, they take body parts of, that is the idea of an scale 2 weapon damage on a scale 1 body.<br /> <br /> A RPG (the weapon, not the game) is an explosive and it is a bit weird on how it works, because it\u2019s cause damage on large areas, but not an absurd damage to parts, like a grenade, but launched at high speeds (possibly with some kind of armor piercing head to penetrate walls without exploding before). A Mortar is the same, it\u2019s a grenade launched in an area far from the launcher, possibly exploding in the air, if desired. As a general rule, explosives don\u2019t have scale rules, they just explode and follow the indirect damage rules, a \u201chigher scale\u201d explosive just have a higher DR and possibly a higher area of effect.<br /> <br /> Aberrant weaponry is not about regular weapon, it\u2019s Super Science, and it uses powers to increase the effectiveness of the equipment. A Super Tech pistol is not a gun you can find in real world, it\u2019s a hand cannon that can only exist due the fact a Nova developed some kind of material or technology that can cause this kind of damage, we are talking about bullets doing Mach 8, or firing singularities, or bullets the size of a fist traveling at bullet speed, if it\u2019s Physical damage, and so it can be what ever scale you can build them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Scale is something people do everyday when they get in their car that has a scale of 2 speed. Normal people interact with doors of wood or steel. People do construction and use wrecking balls. <br /> <br /> The descriptions for scale literally give a pistol at scale 2. Why if it is supposedly scale 1? Why say weapons get increased scale when they dont according to you. <br /> <br /> The Explosive tag doesnt mean indirect damage rules are used. So Ive got no idea where you got all of that.<br /> <br /> Dealing with the rocket launcher and other weapons. It is actually is deadly if it is at the scale described in TC, it's at either scale 3 or 4. Which makes sense. <br /> <br /> The first weapon example in the TC Core, literally doesnt make sense if there is no scale to the weapon. Why does it get points of 8 tags? <br /> <br /> Aberrant is just as much about F-22's dog fighting flying novas as it is super science. In fact the complexity of the rules means most players wont touch them either. but that is tangential. Super science requires you to know what the base scale of the item your crafting is as you get additional tags. A Nova-tech knife isnt as strong as a nova-tech nuke of the same rank. <br /> <br /> The fact is that scale is more important than most tags.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T09:41:15-07:00","id":1451681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451678#post1451678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It DOES say. It says &quot;The access connection is the equipment or specialized space (e.g., lab, darkroom, gym) related to the Path,&quot; pg. 40. It's part of every path. IT is any equipment related to the Path. You're not going to get a laundry list of items or &quot;characters should start with $10,000 worth of equipment per a dot of Wealth&quot;. You're going to start with the equipment it <b>makes sense</b> for your character to have based on their Paths. If your table can't figure out what equipment it makes sense for a member of the military, a hot shot lawyer, a gentleman thief, or an overly protective house husband to have at the beginning of the game, then you need to have a long talk with your table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And how do you make those weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:19:42-07:00","id":1451685,"title":"","content":"I don't. I start with them. I guess if maybe my Path was Gunsmith to the Stars, I might have made it in the past, but most people do not make their own starting equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:25:03-07:00","id":1451686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451678#post1451678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It DOES say. It says &quot;The access connection is the equipment or specialized space (e.g., lab, darkroom, gym) related to the Path,&quot; pg. 40. It's part of every path. IT is any equipment related to the Path. You're not going to get a laundry list of items or &quot;characters should start with $10,000 worth of equipment per a dot of Wealth&quot;. You're going to start with the equipment it <b>makes sense</b> for your character to have based on their Paths. If your table can't figure out what equipment it makes sense for a member of the military, a hot shot lawyer, a gentleman thief, or an overly protective house husband to have at the beginning of the game, then you need to have a long talk with your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>So explain to me, in small words, why there is a section called Weapon Design, under Weapons, that tells me exactly what weapon tags I get?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:38:34-07:00","id":1451689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451686#post1451686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So explain to me, in small words, why there is a section called Weapon Design, under Weapons, that tells me exactly what weapon tags I get?</div> </div> </div> </div>So you can design your own weapons. Just because you can design your own weapons doesn't mean you can't start with the items your Paths' access give you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:41:28-07:00","id":1451690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451689#post1451689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you can design your own weapons. Just because you can design your own weapons doesn't mean you can't start with the items your Paths' access give you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So where are the Weapon Design rules for Paths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:51:14-07:00","id":1451693,"title":"","content":"There aren't any different ones. The GM (and the table) can figure out what tags a weapon from a path should have. If you're playing an Army MP, you probably have an assault rifle. If you're a housewife, you probably have a crappy 1 enhancement knife with the Grapple tag. A hard-boiled detective will probably have a revolver with 1 enhancement and the Ranged: Short tag. You can use the weapon design rules to create the weapons, but Wealth is not a thing in this case; so you can just ignore it. After all, if you're being loaned a gun by the US Government, you're using their Wealth, and it's well over 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:08:05-07:00","id":1451696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451693#post1451693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There aren't any different ones. The GM (and the table) can figure out what tags a weapon from a path should have. If you're playing an Army MP, you probably have an assault rifle. If you're a housewife, you probably have a crappy 1 enhancement knife with the Grapple tag. A hard-boiled detective will probably have a revolver with 1 enhancement and the Ranged: Short tag. You can use the weapon design rules to create the weapons, but Wealth is not a thing in this case; so you can just ignore it. After all, if you're being loaned a gun by the US Government, you're using their Wealth, and it's well over 5 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let me see if I'm understanding you correctly:<br /> Ignore the rules. They don't make sense and you shouldn't use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:09:35-07:00","id":1451698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451696#post1451696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So let me see if I'm understanding you correctly:<br /> Ignore the rules. They don't make sense and you shouldn't use them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are not understanding me correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:13:21-07:00","id":1451699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451698#post1451698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You are not understanding me correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is. Wealth is 0-5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:21:13-07:00","id":1451702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451699#post1451699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is. Wealth is 0-5</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot &quot;not applicable (N/A).&quot; Which is to say, The Wealth edge does not apply here because the Path access is not a character, it's a feature of the Path, and Path features can't have edges. It's like trying to apply for a drivers license for your car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:21:44-07:00","id":1451703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451698#post1451698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You are not understanding me correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what exactly do you mean by &quot;You can use the weapon design rules to create the weapons, but Wealth is not a thing in this case; so you can just ignore it.&quot;? Those are literally the only rules for Weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:26:20-07:00","id":1451705,"title":"","content":"I mean <b>when you are using the access feature of your Path, you can do not use the limits Wealth puts on tags on the weapon because path features don't have the capability of even having the Wealth edge.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:32:45-07:00","id":1451706,"title":"","content":"Thats odd way of fixing the problem of the rules being obtuse; completely rewriting them to make less sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:37:48-07:00","id":1451710,"title":"","content":"I don't think the rules are the obtuse things here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:47:40-07:00","id":1451711,"title":"","content":"Hey Florin, how does the assault rifle have 8 tags?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:54:05-07:00","id":1451714,"title":"","content":"How? They put 8 tags on it. Why? I can't say. Could be a typo, math error, or leftover from a previous iteration. Could be they thought it should have those tags and decided to put in an example to show you don't need to slavishly follow the weapon creation guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:59:30-07:00","id":1451715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451714#post1451714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How? They put 8 tags on it. Why? I can't say. Could be a typo, math error, or leftover from a previous iteration. Could be they thought it should have those tags and decided to put in an example to show you don't need to slavishly follow the weapon creation guidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wow. <br /> <br /> Ok, I'm sure all the mistakes are intentional to show you to believe in yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T12:07:32-07:00","id":1451717,"title":"","content":"I listed 4 options, one of which was it was intentional. The other 3 were versions of &quot;it was a mistake.&quot; But sure, interpret how you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T14:16:15-07:00","id":1451743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451645#post1451645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy do you have anything to support that? Because it says extension not revision.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451648#post1451648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Where is this stated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrante 2e, p. 162. It says neither &quot;extension,&quot; or &quot;revision,&quot; but rather that Aberrant uses a more strictly codified iteration of Scale than default TC, including more specific Scale types and more distinct example of where things fall within them.<br /> <br /> In default TC when a gun moves you from Scale 1 to Scale 2 is left vague to fit the tone of the individual instance of the game. In Aberrant personal firearms have a power Scale of 2, as stated in Aberrant's chart on the matter.<br /> <br /> Also, while Wealth is rating from 0-5, a character (let alone a nation's) practical Wealth rating can be higher via additional Edges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451671#post1451671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't say what equipment, and my question is, what equipment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever makes sense for how your Path(s) are defined, and if necessary how many successes you get on your access connections roll.<br /> <br /> TC isn't a game where you're going to get handed a specific list here, you're expected to collaborate as a group and use those guides to generate an enjoyable result.<br /> <br /> I notice you skipped my question about getting a computer. So, what's you're answer? Or are you ducking it because you know you can't answer it without acknowledging the flaws in your unwillingness to actually listen to explanations?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From my own personal experience, I know plenty of criminals who simply own a gun and have no dots in Wealth and don't particularly owe anyone for the gun. </div> </div> </div>They got the gun from somewhere, right? So either they don't owe someone anymore, or they did something else like steal it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you CAN'T seem to be able to do is stat up a criminal who has a pistol tucked into their pants. </div> </div> </div>I can just fine actually. If I'm the SG, it would go something like this:<br /> <br /> Player of a character with a criminal Path of some sort: &quot;I want my character to start with a pistol because they're a criminal and they'd get one.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Sure, did you take the Wealth Edge or just want it from your Path?&quot;<br /> P: &quot;Path.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;OK, tell me how they got the pistol.&quot;<br /> P: &quot;The guy that recruited my PC into a gang gave it to him for his first big job after doing a bunch of low level stuff.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Cool, show me what tags you want it to have.&quot;<br /> P goes a bit overboard with tags IMO: &quot;Here.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;That seems like too much of a gun for something being handed to someone on their first armed crime, lets either cut it back, or it's going to have some serious complications attached to it.&quot;<br /> P: &quot;Lets just trim some tags.&quot;<br /> <br /> Weapon stating complete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Insofar as the rules say anything, that's what it looks like they say. </div> </div> </div>Can you acknowledge that, even if you feel this is the most &quot;technically correct&quot; reading to you, that such a counter-intuitive result - non-weapon/armor/vehicle items maintain all their bonuses if not purchased with permanent Wealth, but those specific items would literally change in mechanical function based on who owns them - should indicate that you should approach it in a less technical parsing fashion and a more holistic interpretation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just saying something, &quot;going over it,&quot; isn't helpful. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you actually want help. You are literally making up rules to complain about them (you are making up a rule that says weapons obtained from a Path can't be custom designed with tags and have to be from the example table). The only response to you making up a rule is to point out that it isn't what the book says. That's the only helpful thing to be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm looking for information... </div> </div> </div>See, that's the problem here. You're having a debate about how to interpret a text, but you're treating your reading of the text as a &quot;fact&quot; and you're trying to get people to provide &quot;facts&quot; but any alternate interpretation of the text is &quot;not-fact&quot; to you, and thus not information.<br /> <br /> If you want to get a better understanding of the rules, stop looking for &quot;information&quot; because that's not what this is really about, and just trying to actually listen to people instead of setting yourself up to be &quot;discouraged&quot; that you're lack of willingness to listen to what people are saying hasn't magically resulted in you changing your mind on things.<br /> <br /> This isn't about presenting the best &quot;information&quot; to score theoretical system mastery points, this is about presenting the best interpretation of the game to have fun with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know what you think you've said, but &quot;here's how Paths might give a starting character a gun of a certain calibre&quot; is definitely not one of them. </div> </div> </div>And that's just shifting the goal post of what was being responded to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know, at no point have I attempted to perform a psychological analysis of you or your motivations, and I would like the same courtesy in return. </div> </div> </div>If you want more courtesy, consider your own posting habits.<br /> <br /> You're acting like someone that hate pizza, but decided to go to a pizza party, and then spends the whole time trying to get people to explain why the like pizza so you can rant about how wrong they are. Why should we be nice to you about that? If you don't think you're being like that? Maybe you need to reset and start over because you're not really reading the room here as it were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's really just #2. </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't, and insisting it is is the exact sort of rhetorical stubborness that makes you come off as &quot;pizza-hater at a pizza party,&quot; person instead of, &quot;I'm really struggling to understand this please help,&quot; person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you understand the problem I'm having? </div> </div> </div>You're completely unwilling to accept that TC offers multiple ways to use the rules to get the same result. That's the problem you're having. If you let go of the idea that these are meant to be some sort of single unified interwoven equipment rules, and just deal with the fact that Paths, Wealth, and plot are all different ways to get gear that aren't meant to constrain each other, you'd be open to see how they support the game with multiple options,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you mean something other than that? </div> </div> </div>Your instance on hyperbolic jumping to &quot;there are no rules!&quot; tells me that you're smart enough to not just call us all fucking morons for not bowing to how insightful you are because forum rules, but not smart enough to realize how much it comes off that way in your posts anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, rude. </div> </div> </div>From my perspective, I'm being exceedingly patient for the extremely negative attitude you're applying to this conversation.<br /> <br /> What I am, is someone that doesn't really like the white lies of faux niceness where people pretend too be civil in their words, but it's clear their intent lacks any real civility behind it. And yes, it isn't that great in social settings because it's rude to call people out on it because social situations have a strong bias towards enforcing the status quo of civil appearances over penalizing honest communication. There you don't even have to armchair analyze me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe your explanations just suck and only make sense to people with your background of experiences. Or maybe your explanation seems to be to just ignore the most pertinent section of the rulebook, and beef up one of the vague-iest sections of the rulebook, and you don't understand why my brain violently rebels against what you seem to be saying because it's such a useless response. </div> </div> </div>So, what about you in all this? Maybe your questions suck for getting the answers you're looking for. Maybe what you think is pertinent is irrelevant. Maybe your brain is violently rebelling irrationally and the only problem is you keep listening to that instead of realizing maybe you need to tell your brain to quiet down and listen for a bit.<br /> <br /> This isn't a one-way thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the rule is supposed to be &quot;you have what your Paths suggest&quot; why aren't there two sentences supporting that in the rulebook? </div> </div> </div>There are, they've been cited for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does the whole Weapon Design section of the rulebook contradict that? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, you're making up qualifications on the rules to bring them into conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is the purpose of the Weapon Design section if the rules you suggest, the Paths rules, give ZERO guidance on what and how many weapon tags the weapon you acquire should have? </div> </div> </div>I've both already address what the purpose of the Weapon Design section is even with Paths granting equipment, and how the access connection rules do give you guidance on how good you weapon should be.<br /> <br /> If you don't want me to just repeat myself endlessly, how about coming up with new questions instead of just asking the same ones over and over when you're going to reject the answers (even if they're factually true and not a matter of interpretation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T14:21:17-07:00","id":1451746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451710#post1451710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the rules are the obtuse things here.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't insult fellow posters. Also, leave the thread.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T16:06:06-07:00","id":1451766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451743#post1451743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tells me that you're smart enough to not just call us all fucking morons for not bowing to how insightful you are because forum rules, but not smart enough to realize how much it comes off that way in your posts anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chill. <br /> <br /> <br /> To deal with the actual points. <br /> <br /> If aberrant offers only a codification, its not necessarily changing what the scale was at previously but solidifying what was pre existing. As I mentioned, I play only aberrant and only care about that one game, and I need to understand the rules of the game I run. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451743#post1451743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while Wealth is rating from 0-5, a character (let alone a nation's) practical Wealth rating can be higher via additional Edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>------What? Where? Nothing says anything to this effect. You surely mean inspired edges or house rules? <br /> <br /> But nope. The inspired edges in the book dont interact with item creation. <br /> You obviously can make up whatever you want but point that out first. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451743#post1451743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've both already address what the purpose of the Weapon Design section is even with Paths granting equipment, and how the access connection rules do give you guidance on how good you weapon should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are wrong though and your evidence isn't conclusive. <br /> The rule literally say that how you build weapons. They dont say the DM builds weapons in a different way, which it would since it does explicitly say for npcs. <br /> <br /> but then you also say <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451743#post1451743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Player of a character with a criminal Path of some sort: &quot;I want my character to start with a pistol because they're a criminal and they'd get one.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Sure, did you take the Wealth Edge or just want it from your Path?&quot;<br /> P: &quot;Path.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;OK, tell me how they got the pistol.&quot;<br /> P: &quot;The guy that recruited my PC into a gang gave it to him for his first big job after doing a bunch of low level stuff.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Cool, show me what tags you want it to have.&quot;<br /> P goes a bit overboard with tags IMO: &quot;Here.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;That seems like too much of a gun for something being handed to someone on their first armed crime, lets either cut it back, or it's going to have some serious complications attached to it.&quot;<br /> P: &quot;Lets just trim some tags.&quot;<br /> <br /> Weapon stating complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that the DM builds all weapons according to the weapon guides? <br /> <br /> I dont understand your point.<br /> <br /> Mine is that weapon scale needs to be actually addressed my the devs because i see the rules as being vague. Yet ever question but that is answere. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T16:23:36-07:00","id":1451769,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Manifoldpersona;n1451766]Chill.[/quote<br /> <br /> Ah yes, the good old, &quot;don't act mad because I kicked you in the nuts,&quot; approach to conversations.<br /> <br /> If you want people to be chill, don't do unchill things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I mentioned, I play only aberrant and only care about that one game, and I need to understand the rules of the game I run. </div> </div> </div>Then you have your answer? I'm not sure what the point on harping on Scale is if Aberrant is all you care about, and Aberrant has specific Scale rules that address the issue you have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ------What? Where? Nothing says anything to this effect. You surely mean inspired edges or house rules? </div> </div> </div>Have you looked at the Loaded Edge and the Vehicle cost rules?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are wrong though and your evidence isn't conclusive. </div> </div> </div>Which is it?<br /> <br /> Am I clearly wrong? What's <b>your</b> evidence of that? You not finding my evidence conclusive doesn't mean I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rule literally say that how you build weapons. </div> </div> </div>If you want to get weapons that way, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They dont say the DM builds weapons in a different way, which it would since it does explicitly say for npcs. </div> </div> </div>... that doesn't make any sense. If the book says you build weapons in a different way for NPCs... it's saying that the SG builds weapons in a different way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You say that the DM builds all weapons according to the weapon guides? </div> </div> </div>Did you see me, as the SG, build the weapon in that example? Because the player clearly did, and I only exercised my role as SG to ask them to change things to fit the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont understand your point. </div> </div> </div>It wasn't actually addressed to you you know, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mine is that weapon scale needs to be actually addressed my the devs because i see the rules as being vague. Yet ever question but that is answere. </div> </div> </div>Aberrant has weapon scale less vague. It's addressed in that book for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T06:00:40-07:00","id":1451981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451705#post1451705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean <b>when you are using the access feature of your Path, you can do not use the limits Wealth puts on tags on the weapon because path features don't have the capability of even having the Wealth edge.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So where in the rules does it say how to stat up weapons for characters without using the Wealth tag?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26881-pawsplay","name":"pawsplay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T06:42:56-07:00","id":1451986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pawsplay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451981#post1451981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So where in the rules does it say how to stat up weapons for characters without using the Wealth tag?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t. But building weapons with Wealth dot costs, and acquiring weapons via Paths, are two different things that don\u2019t have to be the same. Or to put it another way, you can make a weapon that costs 3 dots. A character with Wealth 3 can purchase that weapon. Another character with a relevant Path can use the Path to gain acquire the weapon without needing to purchase it. Once the game starts, you\u2019re using Path Access to get the weapon. If you want, you could apply a Difficulty or Complication to the roll, to represent the high cost or rarity of the weapon/item you\u2019re trying to acquire. But before the game starts, there are no rolls and you don\u2019t need to test whether you get access - you just get things that make sense for your Path. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m trying to approach this from the point of view that you\u2019re genuinely confused, but your attitude comes across as being deliberately ignorant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T12:33:12-07:00","id":1452033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377726-wealth-and-the-absurd-sparsity-of-weapon-tags?p=1451986#post1451986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn\u2019t. But building weapons with Wealth dot costs, and acquiring weapons via Paths, are two different things that don\u2019t have to be the same. Or to put it another way, you can make a weapon that costs 3 dots. A character with Wealth 3 can purchase that weapon. Another character with a relevant Path can use the Path to gain acquire the weapon without needing to purchase it. Once the game starts, you\u2019re using Path Access to get the weapon. If you want, you could apply a Difficulty or Complication to the roll, to represent the high cost or rarity of the weapon/item you\u2019re trying to acquire. But before the game starts, there are no rolls and you don\u2019t need to test whether you get access - you just get things that make sense for your Path.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m trying to approach this from the point of view that you\u2019re genuinely confused, but your attitude comes across as being deliberately ignorant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So we build all weapons using the Weapon Creation guide. Got it. <br /> <br /> where do the tags come from on the assault rifle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:49:30-07:00","id":1452050,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\">We're done here.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}